# The React Native commit CI builds against.
#
# This project tracks React Native `main` -- ReactCxxPlatform carries no API
# stability guarantee, and half the work here is keeping up with it. That is
# fine for development and useless for CI: a build that follows main turns every
# upstream change into a red tick on an unrelated pull request, and the signal
# stops meaning anything.
#
# So CI pins, and a separate scheduled job tracks main to notice drift on its
# own schedule. Bump this after checking the tree still builds against a newer
# commit -- that bump is the interesting change, and it should be reviewable on
# its own.
b830082cf5cde212e640ae2c1279918076648e90
